# A tag's output constructor as a function value (rulings since the Bible, AN: `Ui.Button.
# Output click`; a constructor is a function, Type System ch. 2): `Each cs,
# Ui.Button.Output` makes an answer of each click. Pins the back end's guard "the answer
# constructor of no tag or with no argument" (lower/expr.prism). Written by Claude on the
# claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

Answers: fn [Click] -> [Output Ui.*]
fn Answers cs = Each cs, Ui.Button.Output

@main: @unit
@main:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{Len (Answers [[click, click]])} answers")   # 0
